WEBVTT

00:02.150 --> 00:03.350
So on that note...

00:03.350 --> 00:07.470
I've called in a veteran maid 
to instruct you in how to serve people!

00:07.470 --> 00:10.480
I'm Lene. I look forward 
to working with all of you.

00:10.480 --> 00:12.770
J-Just a moment, commoner!

00:12.770 --> 00:15.570
Who gave you permission to 
use my servant this way?!

00:15.570 --> 00:18.770
Not her. I asked her to 
find us an instructor.

00:18.770 --> 00:19.830
You did?!

00:19.830 --> 00:25.080
We don't know the first thing about stuff 
like service and assisting customers.

00:25.080 --> 00:26.850
That's true.

00:26.850 --> 00:29.160
If we went into the Foundation 
Day Fair without practicing,

00:29.160 --> 00:30.680
we'd blow it for sure.

00:30.680 --> 00:32.550
Yeah, so there you go.

00:32.910 --> 00:34.520
We're counting on your help.

00:35.860 --> 00:40.180
Um, as you all know, I am a commoner.

00:40.790 --> 00:46.850
I'm sure there are some among you 
who loathe the idea of being taught by me.

00:46.850 --> 00:49.650
But if you remain hung up on status,

00:49.650 --> 00:52.210
you'll never be able to 
serve customers properly.

00:52.210 --> 00:55.570
So until the Foundation Day Fair...

00:57.440 --> 00:59.950
I will have you refer to me as "Instructor."

01:01.700 --> 01:04.080
Lene! That's going too far!

01:04.080 --> 01:07.570
What, so a commoner like you 
is going to order us around?!

01:07.570 --> 01:09.450
I see no problem with it, Dede.

01:09.450 --> 01:10.840
But, Prince Yu...

01:11.200 --> 01:13.090
<i>Ah, that guy.</i>

01:13.590 --> 01:17.930
<i>I guess even servants to the 
royal family are still nobles.</i>

01:19.250 --> 01:21.500
Very well, then.

01:21.500 --> 01:24.070
We're all counting on your guidance, Lene.

01:24.070 --> 01:25.450
Miss Claire...

01:25.850 --> 01:28.480
You mean "<i>Instructor</i> Lene."

01:28.870 --> 01:32.610
Service is giving all for your master 
and expecting nothing in return!

01:32.610 --> 01:35.740
In other words, it is a beautiful 
spirit of compassion!

01:36.320 --> 01:38.740
Read this, and respond when I speak!

01:38.740 --> 01:40.510
Yes, Instructor Lene!

01:40.510 --> 01:42.160
What is the essence of maid work?!

01:42.160 --> 01:44.750
Service and devotion, Instructor Lene!

01:44.750 --> 01:46.290
The first building block of maid work?!

01:46.290 --> 01:48.250
The greeting, Instructor Lene!

01:48.250 --> 01:50.750
Very good! Now, all together!

01:50.750 --> 01:53.020
Welcome home, Master!

01:53.020 --> 01:54.070
I can't hear you!

01:54.070 --> 01:56.130
Welcome home, Master!

01:56.130 --> 01:57.630
Put your hearts into it!

01:57.630 --> 02:00.010
Welcome home, Master.

02:01.280 --> 02:04.140
Welcome home, Master.

02:02.370 --> 02:04.930
Rae! Brother! You don't get 
to get out of this!

02:05.400 --> 02:07.310
Come on! Everyone together!

02:07.310 --> 02:12.040
Welcome home, Master!

02:14.760 --> 02:16.940
What an ordeal that was.

02:16.940 --> 02:20.150
I never knew you had that side to you, Lene.

02:20.150 --> 02:23.950
I'm very sorry. I did get a bit too zealous.

02:24.360 --> 02:27.910
Then again, you've always been 
different from the other maids,

02:27.910 --> 02:31.930
ever since you first came here.

02:32.800 --> 02:36.610
This is the new maid who'll 
be serving you personally.

02:36.610 --> 02:38.560
Go on, introduce yourself.

02:38.560 --> 02:40.650
My name is Lene Aurousseau.

02:40.650 --> 02:42.390
It's my pleasure to serve you.

02:42.390 --> 02:45.020
I don't care what your name is.

02:46.100 --> 02:50.100
You're just going to quit 
within a week, anyway.

02:51.520 --> 02:54.420
No other maids lasted long, huh?

02:54.420 --> 02:55.400
Nope.

02:55.400 --> 02:59.310
Since her parents were busy 
and away from home all the time,

02:59.310 --> 03:02.540
they were all much too soft on Miss Claire.

03:02.540 --> 03:05.710
None of them could deal 
with her selfish whims.

03:06.560 --> 03:07.620
Commoner!

03:07.620 --> 03:09.870
My name is Lene, Miss Claire.

03:09.870 --> 03:12.710
I told you, I don't care what your name is!

03:12.710 --> 03:15.000
What I want you to do 
right now is be a horse!

03:15.430 --> 03:16.930
A... horse?

03:16.930 --> 03:18.750
You don't even know what a horse is?

03:18.750 --> 03:21.130
Really! This is the problem with commoners!

03:21.130 --> 03:25.260
No, I know what a horse is, 
but why must I be one?

03:25.260 --> 03:28.410
Because I want to ride on one, obviously!

03:28.410 --> 03:31.140
Now hurry up and get on all fours already!

03:34.400 --> 03:37.250
Miss Claire, please 
don't make me be a horse.

03:37.250 --> 03:41.310
Excuse me? Are you saying you're 
not going to do as I command?

03:41.310 --> 03:42.190
Yes.

03:42.190 --> 03:43.040
Why, you—

03:43.040 --> 03:45.500
I could never allow a noble such as yourself

03:45.500 --> 03:49.450
to sit on the back of 
a lowly commoner like me.

03:52.100 --> 03:55.040
For a commoner, you know 
your place quite well.

03:55.450 --> 03:58.710
You might actually have potential.

03:58.710 --> 04:03.380
Very well. I will allow you to be my maid.

04:03.380 --> 04:05.370
Give it your best!

04:05.370 --> 04:06.860
Thank you.

04:11.600 --> 04:14.280
Even at that age, you were 
already so easy—

04:14.280 --> 04:16.210
I mean, adorable, Miss Claire!

04:16.210 --> 04:19.230
Hey! You just insulted me 
and tried to gloss over it!

04:19.230 --> 04:22.600
Well, at any rate, now I know Lene 
has always been this stubbor—

04:22.600 --> 04:24.990
I mean, reliable!

04:25.380 --> 04:28.650
I'll be counting on your help at 
the fair as well, Instructor Lene.

04:28.650 --> 04:30.870
Sure. And Miss Claire...

04:31.990 --> 04:33.300
Naturally.

04:33.300 --> 04:37.000
If I'm going to do this personally, 
I must be the best at it!

04:37.000 --> 04:41.490
All right! Let's show everyone 
what real service is!

04:41.490 --> 04:44.010
Yeah!

06:13.930 --> 06:18.940
<b>Episode 7</b>

06:13.930 --> 06:18.940
<b>What Makes or Breaks a School Fair
Is the Cross-Dressing Café</b>

06:41.460 --> 06:46.120
Hmph. Leave it to a commoner to 
look good in a servant's clothes.

06:46.120 --> 06:48.860
Yay! Miss Claire gave me a compliment!

06:48.860 --> 06:50.680
You're not supposed to be happy about it!

06:50.680 --> 06:52.870
Misha, how's this? Do I look okay?

06:52.870 --> 06:55.660
Yes, it suits you perfectly, Prince Yu.

06:56.110 --> 06:58.020
You look really handsome, too!

06:59.080 --> 07:01.010
Thank you...

07:03.370 --> 07:05.020
We've put together a shift schedule.

07:05.020 --> 07:06.860
You'll rotate between 
serving and kitchen work,

07:06.860 --> 07:09.290
and take breaks in turns.

07:10.490 --> 07:12.320
Isn't it nearly time?

07:12.320 --> 07:15.490
All right! I'm so ready for this!

07:19.810 --> 07:23.010
Welcome home, Master!

07:23.500 --> 07:24.860
Right this way.

07:26.080 --> 07:27.250
Here you go.

07:27.250 --> 07:30.760
Have you decided on your order yet, Master?

07:31.130 --> 07:33.890
Coming right up, Master.

07:33.890 --> 07:37.390
Here are your roast beef sandwiches.

07:38.680 --> 07:41.390
Have you received all the items you ordered,

07:41.900 --> 07:43.340
Master?

07:51.600 --> 07:54.640
Miss Claire, you've been 
requested at table 2.

07:55.160 --> 07:57.450
Miss Claire! Here! Over here!

07:57.450 --> 07:59.680
Come on, you've been requested!

08:00.370 --> 08:02.520
Miss Claire! Service!

08:02.520 --> 08:04.750
Yes, Instructor Lene!

08:05.260 --> 08:09.130
Thank you for waiting. 
Allow me to take your order.

08:10.260 --> 08:13.770
You're really angry at me
and not showing it at all!

08:13.770 --> 08:15.010
I love it!

08:16.090 --> 08:17.230
Commoner...

08:17.230 --> 08:20.180
If you don't give it a rest, I will slap you.

08:20.180 --> 08:22.330
Really? You'll reward me?

08:22.890 --> 08:24.720
Oh, right.

08:24.720 --> 08:27.560
You're <i>that</i> sort of person.

08:28.330 --> 08:30.070
What will you have?

08:30.070 --> 08:34.070
Let's see... I'll have the sandwich 
and crème brûlée set, please.

08:34.070 --> 08:36.950
Would you like a drink with that?

08:37.670 --> 08:39.700
Yes, your tears.

08:39.700 --> 08:41.830
No ridiculous jokes!

08:41.830 --> 08:44.010
So, which drink would you like?

08:44.010 --> 08:48.090
I recommend the "get out of here 
as soon as possible."

08:48.090 --> 08:50.190
I'll have black tea after my meal, then.

08:50.190 --> 08:51.460
With pleasure.

08:51.460 --> 08:54.360
Oh, and give me some of that 
Miss Claire sweetness!

08:54.360 --> 08:56.120
I'm afraid we're all out of that.

08:56.120 --> 08:57.440
Aw...

08:57.440 --> 08:59.300
Will that be all for you?

08:59.300 --> 09:03.170
You did very well. 
I'll pat your head as a reward.

09:03.650 --> 09:05.060
If you'll pardon me.

09:06.610 --> 09:08.300
Excuse me!

09:08.300 --> 09:09.570
Yes, comi—

09:09.570 --> 09:13.070
Uh, can I add something to my order?

09:13.070 --> 09:16.200
I'm not going to forget this, 
I'll have you know.

09:16.550 --> 09:17.940
All is at peace.

09:21.870 --> 09:24.790
Thank you for waiting. Please enter, Master.

09:24.790 --> 09:25.760
Prince Yu!

09:26.160 --> 09:28.270
Um... I need to talk to you.

09:28.270 --> 09:31.260
Would you please hear me out? Please!

09:31.670 --> 09:34.420
Kindly refrain from cutting in line.

09:42.170 --> 09:43.120
Sorry.

09:43.680 --> 09:46.380
Not now. Later, okay?

10:00.570 --> 10:03.450
<i>This is going over even 
better than I expected.</i>

10:03.450 --> 10:05.570
Hello? Someone!

10:05.570 --> 10:06.960
Coming!

10:08.250 --> 10:10.210
Thank you for... waiting...

10:10.210 --> 10:14.210
Took you long enough! How dare 
you make His Highness wait?

10:14.640 --> 10:17.130
Do you have any idea who this man is?

10:17.130 --> 10:20.280
He is the revered crown prince 
of the Empire of Loro,

10:20.280 --> 10:22.960
His Imperial Highness Marcel Loro!

10:22.960 --> 10:24.910
Take his order at once!

10:24.910 --> 10:26.850
I-I'm very sorry.

10:26.850 --> 10:30.860
<i>Yikes, it's Prince Marcel. 
He was in the game, too.</i>

10:30.860 --> 10:33.360
<i>If things go the same way, he's gonna...</i>

10:33.990 --> 10:36.890
Bring me something made with dodo bird.

10:36.890 --> 10:39.010
It's His Highness's favorite.

10:39.810 --> 10:41.240
<i>I knew it.</i>

10:41.670 --> 10:46.400
I'm terribly sorry. I'm afraid 
we cannot provide dodo bird.

10:46.400 --> 10:47.870
What did you say?

10:47.870 --> 10:51.000
It's what His Highness wants! 
Do something about it!

10:51.000 --> 10:55.540
I wish I could, but dodo 
bird is a rare delicacy.

10:55.540 --> 10:59.380
You're unlikely to find it anywhere 
in the entire Bauer Kingdom.

10:59.790 --> 11:01.390
<i>This isn't good.</i>

11:01.550 --> 11:09.140
<b>Prince Marcel</b>

11:02.020 --> 11:05.200
<i>Prince Marcel shows up 
at the Foundation Day Fair</i>

11:02.470 --> 11:09.140
<b>Bring me something made with dodo bird.</b>

11:05.200 --> 11:06.930
<i>to make impossible demands of the heroine.</i>

11:06.930 --> 11:09.140
<i>He's just there to get in the way.</i>

11:09.140 --> 11:15.360
<b>Rod</b>

11:09.460 --> 11:11.480
<i>Normally, one of the romanceable characters—</i>

11:11.230 --> 11:15.360
<b>So sorry to interrupt, Your Highness.</b>

11:11.480 --> 11:14.870
<i>meaning the princes—saves her...</i>

11:15.440 --> 11:18.870
<i>But I never thought all my efforts to avoid</i>

11:18.870 --> 11:21.950
<i>raising their affection levels 
would backfire now!</i>

11:22.890 --> 11:26.600
What do you mean, you can't 
bring any dodo bird dishes?!

11:24.200 --> 11:25.370
Rae...

11:26.600 --> 11:28.610
What insolence!

11:28.610 --> 11:30.390
I simply can't believe this!

11:29.280 --> 11:32.540
Forgive me for interrupting, Prince Marcel.

11:29.540 --> 11:32.920
<b>Speaking in Loronese</b>

11:32.920 --> 11:34.480
<i>Miss Claire?</i>

11:34.920 --> 11:38.750
Ah! You speak fluent Loronese!

11:34.920 --> 12:02.700
<b>Speaking in Loronese</b>

11:38.750 --> 11:40.400
What is your name?

11:40.400 --> 11:42.680
I am Claire François.

11:43.020 --> 11:44.850
Might I offer a suggestion?

11:44.850 --> 11:48.190
We do serve a dish made 
with a very rare sauce.

11:48.190 --> 11:49.930
Would you like to try that?

11:50.970 --> 11:55.330
It's an item that only a select few 
have ever tasted, even here in Bauer.

11:55.330 --> 11:57.440
I'm certain Your Highness will enjoy it.

11:57.850 --> 12:00.430
Very well. I'll trust your word.

12:00.430 --> 12:02.700
I am delighted to hear you say so.

12:03.850 --> 12:05.480
Come, let's go.

12:08.530 --> 12:10.760
Taking care of pigs is exhausting!

12:10.760 --> 12:13.710
This is why I hate these 
upstart new-money countries!

12:14.090 --> 12:18.610
Did you get that? His kind will cave 
if you just butter them up enough.

12:18.610 --> 12:20.150
Make sure you remember that.

12:20.150 --> 12:20.960
I will.

12:21.440 --> 12:25.090
Miss Claire, thank you for helping me.

12:26.310 --> 12:29.350
I-It's not as if I did it for you!

12:29.700 --> 12:32.800
Just go and serve him that egg 
sandwich or whatever already!

12:32.800 --> 12:36.430
I doubt mayonnaise has 
reached that pig's country yet.

12:36.430 --> 12:37.310
Got it!

12:42.480 --> 12:43.860
What?

12:43.860 --> 12:47.620
Oh, nothing. I was just reminded 
of something in the past.

12:52.740 --> 12:57.000
M-Miss Claire... I'm fine with 
just the maid uniform, really!

12:57.000 --> 12:58.610
What are you talking about?

12:58.610 --> 13:03.540
It's unacceptable for anyone who 
serves me not to own a single dress!

13:03.920 --> 13:06.870
Let's see... Show us that one.

13:06.870 --> 13:08.550
Certainly.

13:11.810 --> 13:15.600
Hey! What is a commoner doing here?

13:15.960 --> 13:18.350
This is no place for your kind.

13:18.350 --> 13:19.980
Get out at once!

13:25.360 --> 13:29.350
Has my servant done something imprudent?

13:25.780 --> 14:06.820
<b>Speaking in Loronese</b>

13:29.350 --> 13:32.580
Ah, you speak Loronese?

13:32.580 --> 13:35.220
And at your age? You've had a fine education.

13:35.220 --> 13:37.140
Thank you, Your Highness.

13:37.140 --> 13:39.770
I am the daughter of Dole François, 
the minister of finance.

13:39.770 --> 13:41.400
My name is Claire.

13:44.170 --> 13:45.310
What?!

13:45.310 --> 13:49.070
You say King l'Aussiel is working on policy 
to place more importance on commoners?

13:49.070 --> 13:50.600
That is correct.

13:51.080 --> 13:55.060
I brought her here today as a test case.

13:55.060 --> 13:56.170
Hmm...

13:56.170 --> 14:00.810
If that is the wish of Bauer's king, 
my nation cannot disregard it.

14:00.810 --> 14:03.430
I will overlook this incident.

14:03.430 --> 14:05.620
I am delighted to hear you say so.

14:07.830 --> 14:09.320
Miss Claire...

14:10.110 --> 14:13.870
I'm sorry you had to do that because of me.

14:15.340 --> 14:18.810
Those stupid royals really irritate me!

14:18.810 --> 14:19.810
Miss Claire...

14:19.810 --> 14:22.570
The Empire of Loro is nothing but trash!

14:22.570 --> 14:25.640
How dare he reprimand a member 
of my house? Utter insolence!

14:26.510 --> 14:28.580
Listen to me, Lene.

14:28.580 --> 14:31.140
You are my servant—

14:31.140 --> 14:33.110
the servant of Claire François.

14:33.110 --> 14:36.160
That makes you the highest-ranked 
commoner in this kingdom!

14:36.160 --> 14:37.920
Take pride in that!

14:41.850 --> 14:43.740
Yes, Miss Claire!

14:45.100 --> 14:46.650
Very good.

15:05.510 --> 15:09.220
Rae, it's time to swap out. Take your break.

15:09.220 --> 15:11.560
Th-Thank you.

15:16.970 --> 15:20.060
Oh, Miss Claire. Are you also on break now?

15:22.230 --> 15:25.170
You did a great job handling the customers.

15:25.170 --> 15:26.830
I'm a bit surprised.

15:26.830 --> 15:29.100
Who do you think I am?

15:29.100 --> 15:31.510
I'm the daughter of the minister of finance.

15:31.510 --> 15:34.450
I'm used to putting on a front.

15:34.830 --> 15:38.700
But I still like the usual, 
honest Miss Claire more.

15:39.260 --> 15:41.460
Enough flattery.

15:41.780 --> 15:44.360
What about me is honest?

15:44.360 --> 15:47.050
I'm quite well aware of my own personality.

15:49.720 --> 15:54.820
It makes me sad to see you 
putting yourself down like that.

15:55.290 --> 15:57.800
Putting myself down? I'm not—

16:04.820 --> 16:06.650
What are you doing?

16:06.650 --> 16:10.860
Since we have this opportunity, 
why don't we go explore the fair?

16:11.730 --> 16:14.690
I'll do my very best to escort you.

16:28.050 --> 16:30.860
Miss Claire, where shall we go?

16:30.860 --> 16:33.130
I don't need food or drinks.

16:33.130 --> 16:36.370
I carefully choose what goes into my body.

16:36.370 --> 16:37.640
Really?

16:37.640 --> 16:39.610
Okay, let's do this!

16:44.230 --> 16:45.960
I absolutely will <i>not</i>!

16:45.960 --> 16:48.880
What? So you really are afraid of ghosts?

16:48.880 --> 16:51.110
Th-That is not true!

16:51.600 --> 16:55.110
I just don't put up with talk 
of ghosts because it's so puerile.

16:55.110 --> 16:57.100
Oh, so you'll be just fine, then!

16:58.120 --> 17:00.990
Admission for two students, please!

17:00.580 --> 17:02.620
H-Hey! Commoner!

17:07.880 --> 17:09.330
Miss Claire...

17:09.330 --> 17:11.130
Wh-What is it?

17:11.130 --> 17:13.320
If you're scared, you can hold on to me.

17:13.320 --> 17:15.470
What?! Don't be ridiculous!

17:30.540 --> 17:32.360
I'm exhausted.

17:32.360 --> 17:34.530
Are you all right, Miss Claire?

17:34.530 --> 17:36.790
Should I buy you something to drink?

17:36.790 --> 17:38.360
Y-Yes...

17:38.970 --> 17:41.520
But don't buy anything silly!

17:41.520 --> 17:43.010
Water is just fine!

17:43.010 --> 17:44.180
Okay!

17:56.510 --> 17:59.260
Please help us!

17:59.580 --> 18:00.880
Hey!

18:02.000 --> 18:03.450
You're Rae Taylor, aren't you?

18:03.450 --> 18:07.010
The star commoner who got into the 
Royal Academy at the top of her class?

18:07.010 --> 18:08.770
Huh? Er, I...

18:08.770 --> 18:12.520
I'm Matt, a commoner student 
on a scholarship just like you.

18:12.520 --> 18:14.900
Do you have any interest 
in the Commoner Movement?

18:14.900 --> 18:17.280
We're looking for more supporters!

18:17.280 --> 18:19.340
Oh, this is our flyer...

18:19.340 --> 18:20.600
Foolishness.

18:21.410 --> 18:25.410
What ideas are you trying 
to put in my servant's head?

18:25.410 --> 18:27.930
Claire François...

18:29.830 --> 18:32.990
"A movement seeking equality 
among nobles and commoners"?

18:32.990 --> 18:36.260
Enough of this utter nonsense.

18:36.260 --> 18:37.590
Let's go.

18:45.140 --> 18:48.250
Honestly... I wondered what was keeping you.

18:48.250 --> 18:50.600
You let those fools get hold of you?

18:50.600 --> 18:53.980
I don't think their beliefs are foolish.

18:54.600 --> 18:56.540
Don't tell me you agree with...

18:56.540 --> 19:02.160
But whether I'm a commoner 
or a noble, I'll still serve you.

19:05.160 --> 19:07.390
Oh, right. Miss Claire...

19:07.390 --> 19:10.120
This isn't much, but here.

19:12.430 --> 19:13.690
An amulet?

19:13.690 --> 19:14.670
Yes.

19:14.670 --> 19:17.240
It's a charm to help you realize your love.

19:18.550 --> 19:21.050
I hope things work out 
between you and Prince Thane.

19:23.540 --> 19:26.060
You truly are a strange girl.

19:27.520 --> 19:30.460
I know you're only teasing me,

19:30.460 --> 19:34.210
but you do... love me, don't you?

19:34.210 --> 19:36.020
Yes, genuinely.

19:36.020 --> 19:40.520
Yet you support me getting 
together with Prince Thane?

19:40.520 --> 19:42.030
That doesn't make sense.

19:42.510 --> 19:48.290
Your happiness is more important to me 
than seeing my own love realized.

19:51.430 --> 19:53.180
I know I asked you this before,

19:53.180 --> 19:57.420
but why are you so obsessed with me?

20:00.590 --> 20:03.360
Because you're my heart's savior.

20:04.340 --> 20:07.720
<i>I worked myself to exhaustion every day</i>

20:07.720 --> 20:09.930
<i>and had all kinds 
of pressure weighing on me.</i>

20:09.930 --> 20:12.190
<i>It felt so hard to breathe,</i>

20:12.190 --> 20:14.440
<b>In Convenience
Stores Only</b>

20:12.600 --> 20:14.440
<i>but I couldn't escape.</i>

20:15.030 --> 20:16.440
<i>And amid all that...</i>

20:18.440 --> 20:21.440
<b>Claire</b>

20:18.440 --> 20:21.440
<b>A mere commoner dares try to curry favor with me?
Know your place.</b>

20:31.410 --> 20:35.170
<b>Claire</b>

20:31.410 --> 20:36.240
Miss Claire, I know you don't even know it...

20:38.990 --> 20:40.640
but you saved me.

20:41.760 --> 20:45.630
I saved you? That's ridiculous.

20:45.630 --> 20:48.330
You have no intention of giving me 
a real answer, do you?

20:48.330 --> 20:49.940
We should head back now.

20:49.940 --> 20:52.310
Oh, is it that late already?

20:52.730 --> 20:54.910
In that case, Miss Claire, give me your—

20:54.910 --> 20:57.230
You can stop pretending to escort me now.

20:59.580 --> 21:02.690
You and I are a noble and a commoner.

21:03.120 --> 21:05.790
No more or less than that.

21:08.370 --> 21:09.720
Miss Claire?

21:09.720 --> 21:12.040
Come on, let's get moving already.

22:53.380 --> 22:58.170
Ten sheets of parchment, two bottles 
of ink, one ball of leather thread...

22:58.710 --> 23:00.330
We've got everything, right?

23:00.330 --> 23:01.110
Yep.

23:01.450 --> 23:03.370
I can't believe shopping runs are our job.

23:03.370 --> 23:07.770
They're called "knights," but they 
mainly do odd jobs and office work.

23:07.770 --> 23:09.450
The Foundation Day Fair is an exception.

23:09.450 --> 23:12.490
Gosh, the fair was so much fun.

23:12.490 --> 23:14.200
I had a date with Miss Claire!

23:16.200 --> 23:18.700
That's all fake! You made that up!

23:19.370 --> 23:20.550
Is it true?

23:20.550 --> 23:21.430
You're kidding...

23:21.430 --> 23:24.210
Oh? Looks like quite the commotion here.

23:25.810 --> 23:28.850
Loretta, Pepi, what is this all about?

23:28.850 --> 23:30.010
Miss Claire...

23:30.460 --> 23:35.180
It seems like there was a skirmish 
between a commoner and a noble.

23:35.180 --> 23:37.540
Prince Yu's attendant, Master Dede,

23:37.540 --> 23:40.460
attacked a student in the Commoner Movement.

23:46.570 --> 23:48.440
Miss Claire! We've got a case!

23:49.540 --> 23:51.900
I will solve it, no matter what!

23:51.900 --> 23:55.400
I swear on the name of Claire François—
Wait, no I don't!

23:55.400 --> 23:57.920
But I can't keep going if I'm not teasing you!

23:57.920 --> 24:00.490
Loath as I am to admit it, 
I agree with that.

23:59.450 --> 24:00.960
<b>Episode 8</b>

23:59.450 --> 24:00.960
<b>The Swirling Currents Are All Machinations</b>
